  "id": "COMPOUND:43644 - PROTEIN:5858",
  "verbalization": "Blepharocalyxin D is shown to interact with Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide and (1R,2S,6R,7R,10S,11R,12R,14S)-10,11-dihydroxy-2,6-dimethyl-12-propan-2-yl-13-oxatetracyclo[8.5.0.02,7.012,14]pentadecane-6-carboxylic acid. All these compounds are linked to KB, suggesting a potential mechanism where Blepharocalyxin D may inhibit or modulate the activity of SDR family member 9, which in turn affects KB. The consistent interaction between Blepharocalyxin D and SDR family member 9, along with the shared target KB, supports a mechanistic link. The evidence is robust, with multiple independent pathways pointing to the same target and outcome, reinforcing the possibility of a direct or indirect interaction. The mode of action is inferred through the targeting of SDR family member 9, which is a well-characterized class of enzymes involved in metabolic processes. The integration of these findings suggests that Blepharocalyxin D may exert its effects through a pathway involving SDR family member 9, ultimately influencing KB.",
